[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107606,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "<p>Gynandroblastoma is a composite sex cord stromal tumour with elements of Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour and juvenile granulosa cell tumour.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:39:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107607,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8632/1 Gynandroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107608,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F76 &amp; XH0Q64 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of female genital organs &amp; Gynandroblastoma</p>\r\n<p>2C73.Y &amp; XH0Q64 Other specified malignant neoplasms of the ovary &amp; Gynandroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107609,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> mixed sex cord stromal tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107610,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107611,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107612,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients can present with abdominal pain or distension and androgenic symptoms {29660837; 27751908; 2067122; 32815828}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107613,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The reported patients with gynandroblastoma have ranged in age from 13&nbsp;to 80&nbsp;years (median: 24.5&ndash;28&nbsp;years) {29660837; 32815828}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107614,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107615,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the largest study to date, heterozygous hotspot mutations in the RNase&nbsp;IIIb domain of <em>DICER1</em> were discovered in both tumour components in 3&nbsp;of 16&nbsp;cases, all of which showed an admixture of juvenile granulosa cell tumour (JGCT) and Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour (SLCT). All tumours were <em>FOXL2</em>-wildtype, including 7&nbsp;cases with an adult granulosa cell tumour component, and none showed a mutation within the pleckstrin homology domain of <em>AKT1</em> {29660837}. Several additional <em>DICER1</em>-mutant (but only very few <em>FOXL2</em>-mutant) gynandroblastomas have been reported {26428316; 22296244; 29037807}. Because SLCT is also strongly associated with mutations in <em>DICER1</em> {22187960; 29037807}, and because SLCT has a wide range of heterologous differentiation, there is consideration that gynandroblastoma may represent an alternative morphology of SLCT {32815828}. Gynandroblastoma containing a component of adult granulosa cell tumour seems to be different from pure adult granulosa cell tumour, almost all cases of which harbour a hotspot mutation in <em>FOXL2</em> (c.402C&gt;G p.C134W) {19516027; 27297428}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107616,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are usually unilateral and large. The average tumour size is 110&nbsp;mm (range: 55&ndash;200&nbsp;mm). The cut surface is solid or cystic and pale-yellow or white {14479145}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107617,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Typical tumours are composed of (1)&nbsp;deep purple solid lobules of Sertoli cells, or Sertoli cells growing in nests and cords; (2)&nbsp;small clusters of Leydig cells with abundant pink cytoplasm; and (3)&nbsp;pale nodules containing small clusters of cells and variably sized follicles containing pink flocculent material similar to that seen in JGCT {29660837; 32815828}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107618,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107619,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gynandroblastomas composed of SLCT and JGCT elements show biallelic <em>DICER1</em> loss-of-function and missense RNase&nbsp;IIIb mutations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107620,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a sex cord stromal tumour showing an admixture of Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour and JGCT elements.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>DICER1</em> missense RNase&nbsp;IIIb mutation may be present in tumour tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107621,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours are staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th&nbsp;ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T11:45:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107622,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 269,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours are low-stage at diagnosis. Only rare recurrences have been reported {17197894}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:57:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]